<p>
    This website handles your data carefully. In normal operation the application processes
    <strong>no personal data of visitors</strong>: there are no visitor accounts, no
    data-storing form, and no tracking or analytics services.
</p>

<h2>1 · Controller</h2>
<p>
    Mika (Michael) Ferreira, DP Kayl-Téiteng. Contact:
    <a href="mailto:{{ 'home.contact.email'|trans }}">{{ 'home.contact.email'|trans }}</a>.
    Further details in the <a href="{{ path('app_impressum_en') }}">imprint</a>.
</p>

<h2>2 · No trackers, no consent cookies</h2>
<p>
    This website uses <strong>no analytics services and no marketing cookies</strong>. Only
    the application's technically necessary session is used. There is therefore no cookie
    banner.
</p>

<h2>3 · Fonts</h2>
<p>
    Fonts are served <strong>locally from this server</strong>. There is no connection to
    external font services (such as Google Fonts), and therefore <strong>no visitor IP
    address</strong> is passed on to third parties.
</p>

<h2>4 · Server logs</h2>
<p>
    The server stores technical access data (e.g. IP address, date and time, requested URL).
    This data serves secure and stable operation and troubleshooting and is deleted after a
    short period. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in operating the site.
</p>

<h2>5 · Error tracking (Sentry)</h2>
<p>
    To detect and fix technical errors we use <strong>Sentry</strong>, with servers in the
    <strong>EU region (Frankfurt)</strong>. Sentry is engaged as a processor under a data
    processing agreement and is configured so that <strong>no personal data</strong> (no IP
    addresses, no form content) is transmitted.
</p>

<h2>6 · Hosting</h2>
<p>
    The website and database are hosted with <strong>Hostinger</strong> (Hostinger
    Operations UAB), data centre in <strong>Germany (EU)</strong>. The provider is engaged
    as a processor.
</p>

<h2>7 · Contact by email</h2>
<p>
    Contact is handled via <code>mailto:</code> links — this website has <strong>no contact
    form</strong> that stores data. If you send an email, your message is used only to reply
    to you.
</p>

<h2>8 · Your rights</h2>
<p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>access to the stored data,</li>
    <li>rectification of incorrect data,</li>
    <li>erasure ("right to be forgotten"),</li>
    <li>restriction of processing and objection,</li>
    <li>data portability.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    To exercise your rights, write to the address given above. You also have the right to
    lodge a complaint with the <strong>CNPD</strong> (Commission nationale pour la protection
    des données, <a href="https://cnpd.public.lu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cnpd.public.lu</a>).
</p>

<h2>9 · Changes</h2>
<p>
    This statement will be updated if the processing changes. Last updated: September 2026.
</p>
